{"action": "shared_understanding_confirmed", "at": "2026-08-30T21:10:39+00:00", "data": {"summary": "Commerce owns manual unmanaged availability with In stock, Out of stock, and Available on backorder states. New and legacy products default to In stock. A product's last manual choice remains dormant while Manage Stock is enabled and returns when management is disabled; Inventory state is never copied into it. Manual availability cannot be changed while managed, while the separate managed-product backorder policy remains available. Unmanaged storefront output uses the existing structured status and sellable contract without quantity or low-stock output, regardless of store-wide quantity display policy. This slice adds backend persistence, an authenticated mutation action, unified resolution, tests, and proof; it excludes visual EmDash UI, Inventory changes, live transport changes, Blocks rendering, checkout, and deployment."}, "event_id": "74cb5ac0-7458-4294-a472-b048d6759bce"}
